Migrations live here.

Generate the first one with:

    cd backend
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "initial schema"

Then apply:

    alembic upgrade head

Why this matters: the app previously created its schema with
`Base.metadata.create_all()`. That is fine for a fresh install and useless for
evolving one -- it never alters or drops an existing column, so a deployed
instance silently diverges from the code. Alembic is the mechanism that turns a
schema change into a reviewable, reversible, ordered migration.
